re picked, transported and seated in the required order, each place step's final pose confirmed within its registry position and orientation tolerances, with grasp width within grasp_width_tolerance_m and clamp effort well under max_clamp_effort throughout. The four bystanders (u_green, inverted_u_brown, hex_blue, hex_red) and base2 showed no disturbance monitor fires and negligible (<0.1mm) end-to-end movement, so the ACM-permitted cross-assembly contact channel described in the task does not appear to have been exercised against any bystander. However, base1 -- the fixture itself, never picked -- shifted ~5.2mm in position between run start and run end (see observation obs-001-339a64e1 and the verdict recorded at place_inverted_u_yellow), almost certainly from ACM-permitted part-on-base1 contact during one or more of the four insertions. base1 carries no registry spec/tolerance block, so this could not be armed as a numeric clause monitor and is reported as a qualitative violation of the standing \"base1 is undisturbed\" requirement rather than against a registry threshold. This finding was not corrected during the run and stands at run end, so the run-level verdict is non_conformant notwithstanding that every part's own end-state met its registry tolerance.","run_scope":true,"executor_terminal_status":"completed","findings_during_run":["place_inverted_u_yellow"],"recovered":false},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":33}
